FineWine: msl: rayQueryGetIntersectionCandidateAABBOpaqueEXT returned the opposite

The SPIR-V operation is true when the candidate bounding box is opaque. It was translated to
Metal's is_candidate_non_opaque_bounding_box(), which is true when it is not. The ray tracing
pipeline lowering uses it to decide whether an any-hit shader runs for a procedural hit.

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index 85eb7cc..6677af8 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -10510,7 +10510,8 @@ void CompilerMSL::emit_instruction(const Instruction &instruction)
 	case OpRayQueryGetIntersectionCandidateAABBOpaqueKHR:
 	{
 		flush_variable_declaration(ops[0]);
-		emit_op(ops[0], ops[1], join(to_expression(ops[2]), ".is_candidate_non_opaque_bounding_box()"), false);
+		// The SPIR-V operation asks whether the box is opaque; the Metal function, whether it is not.
+		emit_op(ops[0], ops[1], join("!", to_expression(ops[2]), ".is_candidate_non_opaque_bounding_box()"), false);
 		break;
 	}
 	case OpRayQueryConfirmIntersectionKHR:
